# The single divergence a databricks-client image takes from the base locks, and
# not one of its own: an image built with --warehouse-clients snowflake,databricks
# installs both client locks into one interpreter, so every package they share must
# be one version (gateway/tests/test_toolbelt_roles.py
# test_client_locks_agree_with_each_other). dbt-snowflake caps certifi below
# 2025.4.26 (snowflake-clients.overrides), so this lock holds certifi where the
# Snowflake lock does. Nothing in the Databricks clients needs a newer CA list:
# the only server they reach presents the certificate minted at boot.
certifi==2025.1.31
